course: dictionary
lesson: 14276
title: Nominate: suggesting someone for a role or prize
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To nominate someone means to suggest them officially for a job, a position or a prize. Look at the words around it for clues. «Mia wanted to nominate Sam for student of the week.» Mia is not giving Sam the prize. She is putting his name forward for it.
explain: Nominate can also mean to choose or name someone for a job or duty. «The class will nominate a leader for the trip.» The clues are that the class is picking and a leader is the job. Try the swap check: "The class will choose a leader for the trip" still makes sense, so nominate fits here.
explain: Being nominated is not the same as winning. «The film was nominated for an award» means it was put forward for the award. It may still lose, so always read the whole sentence before you decide what happened.
fact: Nominate means to suggest someone officially, or to choose them, for a job, position or prize.
fact: «Nominate» is a verb: nominate, nominates, nominated, nominating.
fact: «Nominated» means put forward for a job or prize, not yet winning it.
fact: Useful phrases: nominate someone for, be nominated, nominated as.
fact: Grown-ups use it in elections too: political parties nominate candidates, which means they choose people to stand for election.
exercise: «Mia wanted to nominate Sam for student of the week.» What does nominate mean here? | *Suggest Sam officially for the prize | Ask Sam to go home | Give Sam the prize straight away | Forget Sam's name
exercise: «The class will nominate a leader for the trip.» What does nominate mean? | Write a long story about a trip | Stop a leader from going | *Choose or name someone for a job | Buy a ticket for someone
exercise: «The film was nominated for an award.» Which statement is true? | It was thrown away after the show | *It was put forward for the award, and it has not yet won | It won the award and everyone cheered | It was made in the school hall
test: «Our school council will nominate two students to be helpers.» Which word means the same as nominate in this sentence? | *Choose | Break | Forget | Hide
test: Yesterday, the teacher ___ Priya for class captain. Which word fits the gap? | *nominated | nominating | nominate | nominates
exam: Which sentence uses nominated correctly? | *Yesterday the class nominated Ben for the sports prize. | Tomorrow the class nominating Ben for the sports prize. | Yesterday the class nominate Ben for the sports prize. | Every day the class nominates Ben for the sports prize yesterday.
